  "reply_text": "Found one merge-blocking bug:\n\n* **[P1] `topTags` mutates the caller’s array** — `src/tags.js:10`  \n  `.sort()` reorders `tags` in place. Since `sidebar()` builds the cloud before taking `tags.slice(0, 5)`, the “recent” strip shows the highest-count tags instead of the first five tags in the supplied order. This also violates the README’s explicit non-mutation contract.\n\n  Reproduced with input ordered `first, second, third, fourth, fifth, sixth`: the recent strip becomes `second, sixth, third, fourth, fifth`.\n\n  **Suggested fix:** sort a copy of the array, and add tests asserting that `topTags` preserves its input and `sidebar` preserves recent-tag order.\n\nAll four existing tests pass, but none checks input mutation or the recent strip. Reviewed `main...tag-cloud` at `89f074f`; no files changed.",
